Logic :

Try out all possibilities of time period for a day
for hour 0-11  (12)
for minutes 0-59  (60)
12*60 => 720

2 for loop
one is for minutes 
inner loop for hours
count number of bits for hour and minute
add all the number of bits
if number of bits equals turnedOn 
then add that time period in a list
then return list


Code :

class Solution {
    public List<String> readBinaryWatch(int turnedOn) {
        List<String> list=new ArrayList<>();
        if(turnedOn>8){
            return new ArrayList<>();
        }
        for(int minute=0;minute<60;minute++){
            for(int hour=0;hour<12;hour++){
                int h=Integer.bitCount(hour);
                int m=Integer.bitCount(minute);
                if(h+m==turnedOn){
                    StringBuilder str=new StringBuilder();
                    str.append(hour);
                    str.append(":");
                    if(minute<10){
                        str.append("0");
                    }
                    str.append(minute);
                    list.add(str.toString());
                }
            }
        }
        return list;
    }
}
